AB  - The document summarizes research abstracts presented at the Montenegrin Sports Academy 23rd Conference, focusing on innovations and challenges in sports science, medicine, and health. Key topics include long-term athlete monitoring in cycling, curriculum development for sport management education, cardiovascular disease prevention strategies applicable to athletes, and the role of ecological environments in adolescent sports motivation in Montenegro. Additional studies address physical literacy and health in older adults, employment challenges in the evolving European sport sector, psychomotor abilities in military and handball athletes, and gender representation disparities in Albanian sports media. The conference also highlights advancements in sports performance assessment methods, such as GPS-based match running analysis in football and novel jump tests for water polo, alongside interventions improving quality of life in elderly populations. Collectively, these abstracts reflect multidisciplinary approaches to enhancing athletic performance, health outcomes, education, and social aspects within the global and regional sports context. Extracted from the article
