AB  - The article focuses on the concept of "form" in cycling, particularly how it can be quantified and managed through training metrics. It discusses the evolution of training methodologies with the introduction of power meters, which allow coaches and athletes to measure training stress and responses more accurately. Key metrics introduced include Training Stress Score (TSS), Intensity Factor (IF), Chronic Training Load (CTL), Acute Training Load (ATL), and Training Stress Balance (TSB), which together help in predicting peak performance and managing fitness and freshness. The article emphasizes the importance of balancing these elements to achieve optimal performance at critical times, illustrating the advancements in coaching and training strategies in the sport. Extracted from the article
