AB  - The article explores how physical therapists (PTs) use specialized knowledge and personal endurance sports experience to treat and prevent injuries in long-distance athletes. Topics include the common injuries experienced by these athletes such as bone stress injuries and tendinopathies, the multidisciplinary approaches to rehabilitation, and training load management strategies featuring insights from PTs Joel Sattgast, Jason Tuori and Chris Johnson.
