AB  - The article focuses on the Garmin Forerunner 970, a feature-rich multisport smartwatch designed for athletes, especially triathletes, that offers comprehensive performance, recovery, and wellness tracking beyond cycling. It features a responsive 47mm AMOLED touchscreen, five physical buttons, and a customizable interface including Garmin’s ‘Glances’ dashboard for quick access to metrics like training status and heart rate variability. While its wrist-based Elevate Gen 5 optical heart rate sensor can produce inconsistent readings during intense efforts, pairing with a chest strap is recommended for precision. The watch supports full mapping, external sensors via Bluetooth and ANT+, and offers up to 21 hours of battery life with a 5 ATM water resistance rating. Although it cannot fully replace a dedicated bike computer due to screen size and positioning limitations, it excels as a versatile multisport device that monitors activity and recovery continuously. Extracted from the article
