AB  - The article reports on a doctoral dissertation that examines the cardiovascular system's response to endurance, strength, and multimodal exercise programs. The study involved 72 physically inactive male participants who underwent acute and long-term adaptations to these exercise modalities. The findings indicate that endurance exercise induces more significant residual effects on the cardiovascular system compared to strength or multimodal training, while multimodal exercises yield greater improvements in muscle strength. The research highlights the sensitivity of electrocardiographic (ECG) analysis in capturing these training adaptations. Extracted from the article
