AB  - The article reports on the development and evaluation of a deep learning model based on a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) autoencoder for analyzing heart rate variability (HRV) as a non-invasive biomarker of muscular fatigue in endurance athletes. The study utilized 50 HRV recordings from trained runners, applying an LSTM autoencoder to extract nonlinear latent representations of HRV, which were then clustered to distinguish autonomic regulation profiles related to fatigue states. The findings indicate that the model effectively captured HRV dynamics and generated interpretable embeddings, offering a data-driven complement to conventional HRV analysis for monitoring training load and recovery in endurance sports. Extracted from the article
