AB  - The editorial discusses the physiological, anatomical, and sport performance adaptations to concentrated training periods in athletes. It emphasizes the importance of understanding the dose-response to exercise and the need for personalized training methodologies. The editorial also highlights the use of wearable technology and subjective assessments to monitor athletes' responses to training loads. The research topic includes four manuscripts that analyze the dose-response relationship to exercise in improving athletic development, focusing on soccer-specific activities, predictors of on-ice performance in youth ice hockey, complex resistance training methods, and the effects of endurance training on muscle oxygen saturation. Extracted from the article
