AB  - The article discusses the determinants and predictors of High Metabolic Load Distance (HMLD) in professional soccer players, focusing on its relationship with physiological and neuromuscular factors. HMLD, an emerging external load indicator, integrates high-speed running and metabolic stress during matches. The study involved 28 male professional outfield players, with HMLD measured via GPS units. Key predictors identified were Maximal Aerobic Speed (MAS) and Yo-Yo IRT2, a test of intermittent endurance capacity. The regression model, HMLD = -1284.26 + 145.85(MAS) + 0.783(Yo-Yo IRT2), explained 63% of the variance in HMLD. The findings highlight the importance of aerobic power and intermittent endurance in match performance. Extracted from the article
