AB  - "By keeping an eye on your HRV, you can plan your training better", says Powers. It's over for me now; I'm going on the piss for the next two months", Geraint Thomas joked at the end of this year's Giro d'Italia. "HRV is like a unique fitness gauge for your body", explains Jeremy Powers, a retired pro cyclist who now works at Whoop, the wearables brand. "This will allow you to understand your HRV trends and baselines, and observe how different factors like training load, sleep quality, and lifestyle habits affect your HRV.". Extracted from the article
