AB  - The article discusses the differences in mechanical and ventilatory efficiency between trained and untrained runners during a VO2 max treadmill test. The study found that well-trained (WT) runners exhibited greater gross mechanical efficiency (GE) than untrained (UT) runners at specific stages of the test, while ventilatory efficiency (VEf) differed by sex, with males showing higher VEf than females. The results suggest that submaximal measures during a VO2 max test can identify both training- and sex-related variations in physiological efficiency. Extracted from the article
