AB  - The article discusses the construct validity of the musculo-cardiopulmonary exercise test (mCPET) in assessing neuromuscular performance differences between strength and endurance trained individuals. The mCPET measures baseline isokinetic cycling power, aerobic power index, fatigue index, and power reserve during incremental cycling. Strength-trained participants exhibited higher baseline power, lower aerobic power index, and greater fatigability compared to endurance-trained participants, supporting the test's sensitivity to training status. The findings validate mCPET as a tool for quantifying neuromuscular adaptations in different training regimens. Extracted from the article
