AB  - The article reports on a study examining second-by-second changes in heart rate (HR) and heart rate variability (HRV) indices during early post-exercise recovery in trained adolescents. The research utilized data from a graded cycling test to analyze HR and HRV dynamics, including SDNN and RMSSD, using a 60-second moving window to capture rapid autonomic fluctuations. Results indicated that HR declined rapidly during recovery, while SDNN increased significantly, with the HR recovery slope showing a strong independent association with SDNN but not RMSSD. The findings suggest that HRV may provide complementary insights into autonomic recovery beyond HR alone. Extracted from the article
