AB  - The article focuses on the variability of in-season training and match loads among academy rugby league players. A study involving 25 male players quantified both internal and external training loads over an 8-week period, revealing significant within- and between-player variability in metrics such as total distance covered, high-speed running, and sprinting. The findings highlight the necessity for individualized load monitoring to optimize player development and performance while minimizing injury risk. The study emphasizes the importance of integrating various load measures to enhance training prescription and recovery strategies. Extracted from the article
