AB  - Your lactate-threshold heart rate is a better baseline than your max heart rate, which is used in other methods, says Roche, because two runners with the same maximum heart rate can have widely dissimilar lactate thresholds due to genetic or training differences. Whoop Strap, free with membership (from $18/month to $30/month) This 24/7 tracker calculates your recovery based on heart-rate variability, resting heart rate, sleep, and respiratory rate. Know when to ignore heart rate Don't bother tracking it during speed intervals and hill workouts, when your heart rate will climb above your lactate threshold or into the upper limit of Zone 3. Extracted from the article
