AB  - The article focuses on the management of the final training phase before a marathon, called "tapering." This crucial period of 3 to 4 weeks aims to reduce the training load to allow the runner to assimilate previous efforts and eliminate fatigue. Three key requirements are emphasized: gradually decreasing the training volume by 41 to 60%, maintaining the intensity of specific sessions, and reducing the weekly frequency by about 20%. The optimal duration of tapering is recommended to be two weeks according to a meta-analysis of 27 studies. Extracted from the article
