AB  - The article presents the "Trail School" method, developed by Sébastien Cornette, which aims to improve the performance of runners of all levels by following the principle of "running less to run better." This method is based on three pillars: muscle strengthening, technique, and physiological development, while emphasizing the management of training load through five levers. Cornette also offers alternatives to traditional long runs, such as bi-daily training and cross-training, to reduce the risk of injury while optimizing training. Extracted from the article
