AB  - The article focuses on the first issue of the Journal of Australian Strength and Conditioning for 2025, highlighting significant research and literature reviews relevant to strength and conditioning coaches. It features a study on the running demands of women’s Australian rules football, revealing that players cover an average of 7 km per match, which provides valuable benchmarks for coaching. Additionally, a review discusses the periodization of recovery modalities, emphasizing the need for strategic application of recovery techniques like cold-water immersion to maximize training adaptations. Another review addresses the physical determinants of change of direction speed, recommending specific training prescriptions for enhancing athletic performance in team sports. Extracted from the article
