AB  - The article focuses on the use of Apple Watch data to monitor pre- and in-season readiness and performance in elite Australian Rules Football athletes. The study involved 38 male athletes who collected cardiac, metabolic, and sleep data during the 2023 Australian Football League season. Results indicated that metrics such as heart rate variability, resting heart rate, and sleep consistency were significantly correlated with various performance outcomes, including high-speed running and strength measures. The findings suggest that Apple Watch data can effectively inform training decisions and enhance athlete performance through improved recovery practices. Extracted from the article
