AB  - The article discusses stress fractures, a common injury among runners, which primarily occurs in the tibia, forefoot, and femoral neck. It emphasizes the importance of early diagnosis and appropriate treatment, including strict rest and a gradual return to training. To prevent these injuries, it is advised to gradually increase training loads, strengthen muscles, and choose suitable shoes. Finally, a return-to-training protocol is recommended, involving complete cessation followed by a supervised resumption to promote healing. Extracted from the article
