AB  - The article focuses on structuring training to progress from a 10 km to a half-marathon, and then to a marathon. For the half-marathon, training requires an adjustment of volume and intensity, with paces around 80% of the VMA (maximum aerobic speed) and long runs lasting up to 1 hour and 30 minutes. Transitioning to the marathon necessitates an increase in training load, including additional sessions and hill workouts to strengthen the muscles. General physical preparation is also essential to prevent injuries, while long runs should last between 1 hour and 30 minutes to 3 hours, incorporating segments at marathon pace to acclimate the body to prolonged effort. Extracted from the article
