AB  - The article presents a study which evaluated the association between heart rate increase after exercise and changes in heart rate variability (HRV) frequency components in trained juvenile cyclists. The study was participated in by 30 subjects who completed the exercise test that was terminated upon volitional fatigue. An increase in the normalized high frequency components and a decrease in the normalized high frequency components of HRV after maximal exercise were found.
