AB  - The article presents a study that examined heart rate variability (HRV) after a one time set of exercise in experienced endurance athletes, while measuring respiratory sinus arrhythmia independently with the use of measures of ventilatory flow and electrocardiography (ECG) at the same time. A characteristic of tachycardia after exercise was elevated clustering of heart beats during inspiration. This result is supported with a hiked respiratory sinus arrhythmia.
