AB  - This article focuses on training load management in runners, emphasizing the importance of the Acute Chronic Workload Ratio (ACWR) for balancing progression and injury prevention. The ACWR compares the acute load (last week) to the chronic load (average of the previous four weeks) and identifies an optimal zone between 0.8 and 1.3, promoting performance and a low risk of injury. A stable chronic load protects against injuries, while sudden variations significantly increase this risk. The article illustrates with concrete examples the impact of good or poor load management, while highlighting that the ACWR should be integrated into a comprehensive approach including sleep, nutrition, and individualized monitoring. Extracted from the article
