AB  - The article presents time saving indoor training sessions for cyclists who have no more than four hours a week for training, based on a variety of factors including frequency, training load, and efficiency. Topics include three sessions of 60 minutes each including quality endurance, redline and High Intensity Interval Training (HIIT). The article also covers training in hilly areas, binge training when time permits, as well as nutrition guidelines.
