AB  - The article focuses on the importance of the sharpening phase in preparing runners before a competition. This period, which generally lasts two to three weeks, aims to reduce accumulated fatigue while maintaining the runner's physical qualities. Two main approaches are presented: progressive unloading, which involves reducing the training load by 30 to 60%, and assimilation-reactivation, which divides the sharpening period into a week of light assimilation followed by a week of reactivation. The choice of approach depends on the runner's fitness level and feelings, highlighting the importance of self-confidence during this delicate phase. Extracted from the article
