AB  - This article presents the special marathon block session, a twice-daily training method developed by Italian coaches Renato Canova and Luciano Gigliotti, aimed at effectively preparing marathon runners. This session involves running twice a day at specific paces close to marathon pace, with a total volume that can exceed 40 km, in order to improve endurance, the ability to sustain the target pace, and fat-burning capacity, which is essential for delaying fatigue related to glycogen depletion. The training also includes a low-carbohydrate diet between the two sessions to promote the use of fats as an energy source. Adaptations are proposed for different levels of runners, emphasizing the importance of recovery and the personalization of training load. Extracted from the article
