AB  - Perhaps it's because of their Nordic roots that saunas are so popular among skiers, but conduct a Google search or visit a ski club and you'd be hard pressed - aside from icing for injuries - to find a strong connection between cross country skiing and cold therapy. Ever since my time as a high school cross country skier, I've been prone to inflammation. Other studies about continued cold therapy point to additional physiological changes that would benefit competitive skiers, like higher heart rate variability, better cold acclimation and a higher quality of sleep (a vital part of the recovery process). Extracted from the article
