AB  - This article focuses on the use of heart rate (HR) as a training tool for runners. It explains the key concepts of Maximum Heart Rate (MHR), Heart Rate Reserve (HRR), and Heart Rate Variability (HRV), which help to better measure and control the intensity of effort. Heart rate is used to assess performance, adaptation to effort, and recovery, while taking into account external factors influencing this measurement. The article also emphasizes the importance of using accurate equipment, such as a chest strap, and recommends heart rate as a reliable indicator to adjust training, especially for beginners or people resuming physical activity. Extracted from the article
