AB  - The article investigates the relationships among aerobic training status, muscle twitch properties, fatigue rate, and critical torque during electrically stimulated exercise. The study involved twenty participants, divided into aerobically trained and sedentary groups, who underwent a VO2 peak test and an electrically stimulated critical torque test. Results indicated that while the trained group had a significantly higher VO2 peak, there were no notable differences in critical torque or fatigue measures between the two groups. Additionally, significant correlations were found between critical torque and various torque-related measures, suggesting that aerobic training status does not influence critical torque or initial peripheral fatigue during stimulated exercise. Extracted from the article
