AB  - This article focuses on optimizing training load for runners, emphasizing the importance of training volume, particularly in Zone 1 (Z1), which corresponds to a low intensity below 80% of the Maximal Aerobic Speed (MAS). A study analyzing more than 119,000 marathons shows that the fastest runners accumulate a training volume three times greater than that of the slowest runners, mainly in Z1. Polarized training, combining a large volume in Z1 with high-intensity sessions in Zone 3 (Z3, >88% MAS), is presented as more effective than training at intermediate intensity (Z2). Finally, strength training is recommended to compensate for limited training volume, with significant gains in performance and running economy. Extracted from the article
