AB  - The article presents a summary of the study "Effect of intensive training on heart rate variability in prepubertal swimmers," by A. Vinet, L. Beck, S. Nottin, and P. Obert. In the study the authors used heart rate variability to examine possible sympathovagal alterations in highly trained prepubertal male swimmers and compared the results with age-matched nontrained control subjects. According to the article, the study failed to show differences in time or frequency domains of heart rate variability between trained and untrained subjects.
