AB  - The article focuses on the use of session-rating of perceived exertion (RPE) in monitoring the training load (LD) in swimmers. It stresses the importance of the titration of the increases in physical TLs with the corresponding recovery in the optimization of athletic performance. It describes session-RPE as a simple approach for monitoring internal TL under which the intensity of the training session will be rated by athletes. Advantages of session-RPE in measuring TL in swimmers are discussed which include improvement in periodization strategies.
