AB  - Under the background of the increasing number of annual track and field competitions, how to reasonably control the training load, determine the number of important competitions, and promote the athletes to form their best competitive state have become a problem that coaches need to study constantly. This study analyzed the characteristics of 2018-2019 annual training load of Li Ling by the methods of expert interview and case analysis. The main conclu¬sions were as follows. 1) In 2019, Li Ling adopted multi-cycle training and plate?，training mode, which were divided into four training cycles. Through constant adjustment of training loads, Li Ling’s competitive state showed a rising trend, and her best competitive state of the year appeared in the most important competition of this season. 2) Before Shanghai Diamond League，two kinds of pre-competition training methods included “leading competition” and “high-load intensive training course”，were adopted and effectively improved the competitive state of the player. 3) Special physical fitness was the key factor to improve the athletes* run-up speed, the improvement of run-up speed and take off aggressiveness led to the increase the height and weight of the pole, which improved the performance of the athlete. 4) The annual training load changed with the cycle goal and Li Ling9s physical condition. Compared with four periods horizontally, the load showed a decreasing trend, and the first cycle is the largest； the training intensity showed an increasing trend, and the fourth cycle reached the maximum. Compared with different training stages of each cycle, the load characteristics showed that the load changes was in a wave shape, the competition stage was rela¬tively small ； the training intensity continued to rise, reaching the maximum in the competition stage. ABSTRACT FROM AUTHOR
