AB  - Research is presented which examined methods for quantifying training in Sprint Kayak and monitoring the fitness and performance of 10 junior Sprint Kayak athletes with a focus on the session rating of perceived exertion (session-RPE) method and common measures of training load (TL). The study found that session-RPE is a valid method for monitoring TL for junior Sprint Kayak athletes and also supports the use of session-RPE in Sprint Kayak training.
