AB  - The article focuses on the study which develops a method to monitor responses to training loads on an individual basis in the recreational long-distance runners (LDR). The study used individualized training impulses (TRIMP) analysis which determines the lactate profiles during incremental treadmill test and the changes of speed in submaximal aerobic fitness at the end of training intervention. It found that TRIMP analysis is considered a valid tool related to track performance in LDR. Moreover, researchers have observed that there was no significant relationship between any variable was detected when average-based group values is applied.
