AB  - The article reports on research which was conducted to compare the heart rate (HR) and rate of perceived exertion (RPE) responses as internal load indicators while performing duet routines during training and competition in synchronized swimming (SS). Researchers evaluated 10 Olympic swimming medalists. They found that the internal load imposed by SS duets performed during training is virtually identical to that elicited in a real competitive situation and that practicing competitive routines is suitable for developing and maintaining the cardiovascular fitness needed by swimmers.
