AB  - The article reports on a study conducted to evaluate the effect of training load changes and subsequent detraining on purine metabolism in middle-distance runners during a one year cycle. It states in the training cycle, activities including plasma hypoxanthine (Hx) and uric acid, and erythrocyte Hx-guanine phosphoribosyltransferase (HGPRT) were determined the pre and post exercise session. It states during the competitive state training loads in aerobic compensation and threshold zones decreased by 65.4 percent and 20.5 percent respectively.
