AB  - The article reports on research which investigated the autonomic nervous system recovery and psychological response which resulted from three training amplitudes and to determine their relationship with heart rate (HR), heart rate variability (HRV) and rate of perceived exertion (RPE) in rowing. Researchers evaluated eight young rowers. They found that training with higher load variation between effort and recovery impacted HRV, HR, and RPE with greater intensity and that younger rowers were ready for new training sessions 24 hours after either training method.
