AB  - The article discusses the physiological strain from hypoxic high-intensity interval training (HHIT) in highly trained runners. Details on tests conducted to young runners in hypoxic condition which include the changes in neutrophils, blood lactate, and erythropoietin are explored. An overview of the high-intensity interval training (HIT) as the component for endurance training program for runners is also provided.
