AB  - The article presents a study which investigates the association of HR variability (HRV) and illnesses in elite swimmers such as upper respiratory tract, all-type pathologies, and muscular affections. The study made use of spectral analysis and explanatory variables by time domain to assessed the indexes of orthostatic position and cardiac autonomic regulation in supine. The result of the study indicates that national swimmers were high risk for all-type pathologies in winter and decrease of time domain (SD1) and increase low frequency (LF) in orthostatic position were higher risks of muscular affections.
