AB  - The article reports on research which was conducted to investigate the effect different pressure threshold inspiratory loads had on on lactate clearance and plasma acid-base balance during recovery from maximal exercise. Researchers evaluated eight moderately trained male athletes who performed cycling tests. They found that in athletes who had achieved moderate enduring training status, inspiratory loading did not appear to accelerate lactate clearance or modify plasma acid-base balance during recovery from maximal exercise.
