AB  - The article discusses research investigating the training status (TS) and match activity (MA) of professional soccer players throughout a season. The authors analyzed both MA and fatigue development (FD) during official soccer games at various times in the season and examined the influence of TS on MA and FD via time-motion analysis. The correlation between physical fitness variables, composites scores of power-related and isokinetic strength tests with game physical parameters is discussed.
