AB  - The article discusses the improvement on boat speeding. Boat velocity increased by two to three percent since 1892, as a result of having taller and stronger athletes. However, the increase in physical dimensions is less than ten percent, while the increase in training load is one third of the increase in physical capacity and performance. Moreover, the reductions in boat drag, increased oar blade efficiency, and improvements in rowing techniques and tools contributed to faster speed.
