AB  - The article presents research on session rating of perceived exertion (SRPE), a method for estimating the physical impact of exercise during physical training for evaluating that training. SPRE was measured for persons engaged in treadmill and cycling exercise of low and moderate intensity. Analysis of variance indicated significantly greater SRPE for higher intensity levels of each form of exercise. It is suggested that the use of SRPE to monitor training is dependent on the form of exercise involved.
