AB  - In this study the authors investigated metabolic and spiroergometric values in 18 cyclists during submaximal exercise test on a bicycle ergometer. Results showed that 3 minute incremental stage tests are not reliable in estimating lactate steady state or predicting performance, and that VO2, training load and heart rate correspond better among different trials than does lactate. The authors conclude that the best way of predicting and monitoring training intensity could be a combination of workload and heart rate.
