AB  - Resting bradycardia in athletes is well documented in cross-sectional studies while the endurance training of sedentary subjects lasting 8-30 weeks does not always result in the decrease of resting heart rate. Attempts to elucidate resting bradycardia mechanism did not unambiguously confirm the commonly held opinion of the role of increased parasympathetic activity. All experiments in which the pharmacological blockade of autonomic system was applied showed decreased intrinsic heart rate in athletes. Many experiments in which analysis of heart rate variability was used for assessment of autonomic nervous system activity suggest increased parasympathetic activity, however the conclusion based on this method should be regarded with great caution.
