AB  - The article discusses heart rate variability, psychological state and performance as possible markers for overtraining syndrome. The authors observed these markers in athletes who are members of an elite squad during a period of overtraining producing the syndrome. Taken individually, the markers were not as sensitive or as specific to reliably predict the onset of overtraining syndrome. Taken together, these measures may have enough sensitivity and specificity to prevent excessive training.
