AB  - In this article one can find the recommendations on methodology as regards the modern swim training destined for the competitors. Taking in account the theoretical and practical knowledge of two outstanding Russian experts in this field - Platonov and Vajciechovskij - the author considers such matters as the training effects on the organism of a swimmer, fatigue and recovery processes, training goals in relation to training loads. Next, he describes two kinds of approach towards a selection of methods, being in accordance with the standpoint of two mentioned experts. In addition he presents his own experience concerning the training curriculum carried out during the preparatory season in the sporting camp for young swimmers (girls aged 14-15 years - advanced juniors). The training guidelines were worked out on the basis of Platonov's and Vajciechovskij's recommendations. The author finds that the positive results were clear after applying the recommended methods during one-week microcycle training.
