AB  - It was observed after two years trial study that the athletic abilities of group cyclists were composed of three main factors of heart output, muscle strength (for working ability) and synthetic ability, while those of the individual cyclists were of their own characteristics. The physical indexes sensitive to speed, endurance and speed endurance also indicated differences between group and individuals and among individuals themselves. The results showed that there were great differences existing among individual cyclists in the adaptation to training load and mutual compensation of physical function. It is thus suggested that individual features should be paid attention to in load arrangement and physical ability control in training.
