AB  - The article investigates the impact of chronic metformin use on insulin resistance and cardiorespiratory fitness improvements from intense aerobic training in individuals with hyperglycemic metabolic syndrome (MetS). A study involving 63 middle-aged participants, some on metformin and others not, revealed that while both groups experienced similar reductions in insulin resistance and improvements in MetS scores, metformin users had significantly lower enhancements in VO2MAX compared to those not on the medication. Despite this attenuation in VO2MAX improvements, metformin did not hinder overall metabolic improvements associated with aerobic exercise training. Extracted from the article
