AB  - The article discusses how different body types respond to high intensity triathlon training. The ability of females to typically train at a higher intensity and tolerate more training load than males is explained. A mesomorph or muscled athlete is described as being unable to tolerate high levels of speed and lactate tolerance work as readily as an ectomorph or skinnier character can. Eating gluten-free food and giving up alcohol are cited as the two most efficient ways to lose weight.
