AB  - The physiological, biochemical and work-load indexes of the women players of the Chinese National Handball Team taking part in the National Championship and the International Invitational Tournament were detected and studied. The results showed that the whole fitness level of the Chinese women handball players was poor, especially the anaerobic endurance. The work-load indexes in the Chinese women handball players were poorer than those of the Korean players. The exercise intensity combined with the distance of running and fast-speed running is a good index, simple and easy operated to evaluate training loads. Applying the Polar heart-rate device to register heart rates showed that the average heart rate could accurately evaluate the intensity of workload. The threshold of the urine protein excretion per minute is an easy and practical index to evaluate training intensity.
