AB  - In the field of research on sport and immunity, there are a lot of contradictory reports of effects of lymphocyte proliferation on mitogen reaction. The effects of different exercises and age factors on lymphocyte proliferation were studied. The results indicated that exhaustive swimming decreased the effects of lymphocyte proliferation on LPS, which, therefore, would be able to hurt the immune function related tobcells. Effects of exhaustive swimming appeared to be unsure in influencing on proliferation activities of T cells, but they were related with the training load and the age of the object. Training of different workload affected T cell proliferation differently. It appeared that the influence of exercise on the proliferation of T cells did not change gradually. The reaction of ConA-induced proliferation on spleen cells was stronger than that of lymphoglandulae mesentericae cells, but both of them trended to change similarly.
