AB  - The article focuses on the effects of different altitudes of training on improving the stamina of middle-distance race athletes. Results show that hematinic chalybeate can help keep hemoglobin in high level during endurance exercise, while the altitude of training can increase athletes' hemoglobin level. It states that the stamina of middle-distance race athletes can be effectively improved by enhancing first training load then increasing exercise intensity in high altitude training.
