AB  - The article looks at how to quantify training load and how to structure individual programs to achieve improvement and development of runners. It proposes the use of the Training Impulse (TRIMP) unit to quantify training absorbed. Factors such as distance run, speed and elevation gained are considered in calculating training loads. Tables show the increased training load by the introduction of two sessions, and by keeping a single session per day but increasing the volume and intensity of runs.
