AB  - The article discusses the importance of tapering training load for competitive runners. Training load reduction gives a runner's body a chance to rejuvenate and adjust to the training experienced by the athlete. While a study revealed that reducing training volume by 60-90 percent can enhance performance of short-race runners, such a high level of training cutdown is ill-advised for marathon runners. A gradual training reduction beginning three weeks before a competition is said to be best suited for long distance runners.
