AB  - In this study speed of run has been defined for two moments in the course of adaptation to the exertion of gradually increasing burden: anaerobic threshold (AT) as well as criterion of lactate concentration equal to 4 mmol.1-1. Six runners were examined representing I and II sports class in the first days of May 1983. The examinations were carried out on mechanical running track. The examined runners performed four 4-minute exertions of gradually increasing intensity, interrupted by 90-second pauses for taking blood. The test was continued with the exertion of intensity increasing every 2 minutes, and finished with the refusal of performing the task. It seems that a precise and objective method of differentiating the scope of intensity of running training would be to utilize speed of run on the AT level as well as lactate concentration equal to 4 mmol.1-1.
