AB  - The training response of eleven Canadian National swimmers (6 males and 5 females) was investigated. These swimmers were tested before and after a six-month training period. Maximum oxygen uptake increased significantly and maximal heart rate decreased significantly for both male and female subjects. It was concluded that cardiovascular adaptations can occur in elite athletes submitted to a severe training program.
