AB  - The author discusses the views of several runners in the 1970's and 1980's regarding the high-volume training sessions of runners. Runner Mike Baxter criticized distance runners for doing track repetitions too slowly resulting from high volume training of each session. According to athlete Cameron Spence, there is something about training at a certain pace that brings about a particular psychological training response. The author points out that one should not be hasty with assumptions regarding athlete Alyson Dixon's training regime.
