AB  - The article defines the term "tapering" as a marked reduction in training load a few days before an important event. The aim is to reduce training and therefore reduce physiological and psychological stress. Evidence suggests that during tapering key hormone balances can be restored, there is a reduction in perception of effort. Feelings of fatigue are also lessened and sleep quality is improved.
