AB  - The authors use a classification of the training methods for sports, characterized by repetitions of rhythmic movements, for defining of the omissions in the planning efficacy. The possibilities for negative influence of a wrong - aimed training plan are pointed out, as well as the necessity of unified sports - pedagogical and biological criteria for stating of definite training loads in the abovementioned sports. The article presents a complete sport-pedagogical model of training and competitional loads, applied in the preparation of middle and long distance runners. The model can be applied in training planning for canoeing, kayaking, swimming, bicycling and rowing, while the drafts of physiological and biochemical regimes might be used for the development of physical characteristics others than speed endurance.
