AB  - The paper presents a synthesis of the results of numerous research projects on the effects of alpine conditions on man's working capacity and performance. The problems of preparation for major competitions (World Championships, Olympic Games, etc.) in lowland conditions through special alpine training are also dealt with. Theoretical considerations are illustrated with the examples of training for women middle-distance runners. Attention is also drawn to the principles of endurance training monitoring under alpine conditions and the essential preventive measures to protect the athlete's body from acute alpine illness.
