AB  - 44 top-class tennis players were put through ergometric tests on a bicycle and treadmill: 1) the heart size, oxygen pulse, maximum oxygen uptake and lactate levels showed favourable adaptation in these tennis players, 2) the optimal training load can be set using the threshold heart rate. Top class tennis players should carry out endurance training at a heart rate of between 160-170/min, 3) the spiroergometric tests, particularly those on the running board provide clear proof of the organic requirements of tennis players. Diagnoses of performance in tennis is however made more difficult by the fact that the performance ability in this sport depends very much upon the technical and tactical ability and general coordination and concentration. These factors cannot be objectively evaluated at present.
