AB  - Author proceeds from many investigations in which the rise of the activity of creatinine kinase in serum was observed in distance runners after exercise. The rise of plasmatic level of nitrocellular muscle proteins after training load depends on the intensity of the load. In better trained athletes, lower rates were recorded and also the recovery period took a faster course. The following changes in the creatine kinase becomes a routine biochemical method which offers the coach a valuable information on the response of organism to the trainng load.
