AB  - A fitness test was described that was elaborated for adult and junior elite water polo players. It consisted of 6x30 m freestyle swimming, 4 minute recovery heart rate measurement and a single 30 m freestyle swimming. Maximal speed, mean time of 6x30 m swims, 4 minute recovery heart rate sum and difference between the first half minute and the second half minute restitution heart rate sum were measured. The swimming performance and the heart rate recovery were described by indices and a further index was counted from them. In 1988 four measurements were done: at the end of the preparation the swimming performance enhanced and the heart rate recovery impaired, the combined index hardly changed during the whole year. The data, measured between 1983-88 were also studied in the function of age. According to the results the swimming performance between 15-21 years improved, between 21-30 years practically did not change while the heart rate recovery grew better from 15 to 30 years.
